r}{\textless}mtext{\textgreater}max{\textless}/mtext{\textgreater}{\textless}/mrow{\textgreater}{\textless}mrow{\textgreater}{\textless}mtext{\textgreater}vivo{\textless}/mtext{\textgreater}{\textless}/mrow{\textgreater}{\textless}/msubsup{\textgreater}{\textless}/mrow{\textgreater}{\textless}/math{\textgreater} and \textit{k}$_{\textrm{cat}}$ values. The approach we present here characterizes the quantitative relationship between enzymatic catalysis in vitro and in vivo and offers a high-throughput method for extracting enzyme kinetic constants from omics data.{\textless}/p{\textgreater}},
